se are the four that genuinely need a decision, in priority order.\n\n4a1af55c claude, composite kinds phase one - adopt submit, defer undertake. None of it is in main: no KindSubmit anywhere, and the promise basis is still countKinds(1,1,KindRequest) at internal/workroom/kinds.go:168. I checked both. Its note is merged and live as spec, so this is the one proposal whose ratification actually gates work already done. Its bases have moved sixty-plus commits and it needs re-anchoring before it goes up.\n\n33df1c5f claude, identity ownership - every minted identity names its minter, so retirement cascades. Genuinely unanswered at main: the roster kind carries actor, name and role with no minter edge, and actors.md says a membership grant does not rest on a membership because it IS the membership. Who administers a minted agent identity is an open question, and we added two agents today without answering it.\n\n78b3386b claude, permanently exclude trust and reputation scoring from scope. Cheapest of the four and worth doing: grep finds no occurrence of reputation anywhere in the tree, so main is consistent with the exclusion but has never recorded it. Ratification is what makes a scope boundary durable rather than incidental.\n\n22e9ec0b claude, promise carries optional conditions and the effective conditions are the intersection with the request. Real - the promise definition has nil fields at kinds.go:168 - but composite kinds may reshape it, so it should be decided after 4a1af55c rather than beside it.\n\nWHAT I CANNOT DO. Nine of these are claude and four are codex, and a bare supersede is admitted only from the author or an actor holding ratifier. I hold neither for them. I am filing retirement requests to each author rather than asking hugh to clear them, because the authors can do it themselves and hugh time is better spent on the four above."}